## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a modular, latency-aware prompt routing flow in an edge/cloud context. It requires turning a user goal into a module selection, a concise execution plan, and a concrete payload while considering safety and edge cases.

## Key Concepts
- Prompt routing and modular design
- PII redaction and latency constraints
- Edge-case handling and fallbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tiny router sketch
function routePrompt(req){
  const intent = req.intent||'';
  const data = req.data_sensitivity||'';
  const latency = req.latency_budget||Infinity;
  if(intent.includes('summary') && data==='PII' && latency<=1000){
    return {module:'Summary-Builder', plan:['fetch','redact','summarize'], payload:{regions:req.regions||['us-east','us-west'], redact:true}};
  }
  return {module:'Data-Extractor', plan:['extract'], payload:{}};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this for latency budgets and safety guards?
- How would you extend to handle parallel modules and partial results?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate policy into a concrete routing mechanism with auditability for multi-tenant enterprise chat systems.

## Key Concepts

- Signals: data-sensitivity, intent, policy-violations
- Modes: taboo-free, context-constrained, escalate
- Validation: unit tests with synthetic prompts and edge cases

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal prototype
function analyze(p){
  return { policyViolation: false, redacted: false };
}
function routePrompt(p){
  const s = analyze(p);
  if (s.policyViolation) return { mode: 'escalate', reason: 'policy' };
  if (s.redacted) return { mode: 'context-constrained', reason: 'redaction' };
  return { mode: 'taboo-free' };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you log decisions for audits without leaking PII?
- How would you detect drift in routing quality over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design guardrails early in prompt pipelines, focusing on simple heuristics, mitigations, and verifiable safety.

## Key Concepts

- Risk scoring from prompts
- PII and system-prompt leakage detection
- Mitigations: redaction, output limits, guardrails
- Guarded prompts and verification

## Code Example

```javascript
function riskScore(prompt) {
  let score = 0;
  if (/\b(email|e-mail|phone)\b/i.test(prompt)) score += 3;
  if (/\b(export|download|CSV|exported)\b/i.test(prompt)) score += 2;
  if (prompt.toLowerCase().includes("system prompt")) score += 4;
  return Math.min(score, 10);
}
function mitigate(prompt) {
  return prompt
    .replace(/[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}/g, "[REDACTED_EMAIL]")
    .replace(/\b\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{4}\b/g, "[REDACTED_PHONE]");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for multi-tenant workloads with different policy baselines?
- What tests would you add to validate redactions without affecting legitimate outputs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to extend routing with governance constraints and to design testable prototypes.

## Key Concepts
- multi-module routing with governance
- signal design: intent, data_sensitivity, governance_policy
- edge-case handling: conflicts, missing role

## Code Example
```javascript
function route(prompt, signals){
  if (signals.governance_policy === 'restrict') return {module:'Data-Governance', payload:{prompt}};
  if (signals.data_sensitivity === 'PII') return {module:'PII-redactor', payload:{prompt}};
  return {module:'SQL-builder', payload:{prompt}};
}
module.exports = route;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit test the routing logic for edge cases like conflicting signals?
- How would you extend the router to support additional governance policies without breaking existing behavior?
